    {
      "text": "%sql\n--See the following customers and orders tables \n--The following example uses the EXISTS operator to find all customers who have the order.\nselect customer_id, name from customers c\nwhere exists(select 1 from orders where customer_id=c.customer_id)\n",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/sql",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "sql",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "e58cd589c43245359ac6f"
    },
    {
      "text": "%sql\n--To get more meaningful data, you can join the orders table with the customers table as follows:\n\nselect\nname,\ncount(order_id)\nfrom orders inner join customers using(customer_id)\nWHERE \n   status = 'Shipped'\ngroup by name\norder by name",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/sql",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "sql",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "4456175fffed40d7bbf82"
    },
    {
      "text": "%sql\n\nSELECT\n    product_id,\n    product_name,\n    list_price\nFROM\n    products\nWHERE\n    list_price > (\n        SELECT\n            AVG( list_price )\n        FROM\n            products\n    )\nORDER BY\n    product_name;",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/sql",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "sql",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "afb0ee4c55fe4bbd95251"
    },
    {
      "text": "###Oracle EXISTS vs. IN\n\nThe EXISTS operator stops scanning rows once the subquery returns the first row because it can determine the result whereas the IN operator must scan all rows returned by the subquery to conclude the result.\n- Typically, the EXISTS operator is faster than IN operator when the result set of the subquery is large. By contrast, the IN operator is faster than EXISTS operator when the result set of the subquery is small.\n\n",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "01cce34ea29b4d67ab861"
    },
    {
      "text": "%sql\nselect order_date,to_date(order_date) as dt, extract(year from order_date) , substring(to_date(order_date),1,4) as year from orders limit 5;",
